  "rationale": "Direct-match hypertension PRS candidates are present (e.g., PGS000706, PGS001320, PGS001838, PGS002047, PGS004234, PGS004236, PGS004191–PGS004194, PGS004934, PGS004785/PGS004787, etc.), so this is not a no-match scenario. Among these, PGS004236 (Hypertension; PRSsum) is best supported in the provided metadata by (i) strong endpoint fidelity (trait_reported/trait_efo/phenotyping_reported all hypertension), (ii) a clearly multi-ethnic development/evaluation context (DEV includes AFR/AMR/ASN/EUR; EVAL is multi-ethnic; validation n=39,035), (iii) relatively clean covariates for comparability (age/age2, sex, site, race/ethnic background, smoking, BMI, PCs) without obvious near-outcome biomarkers or risk-calculator packaging, and (iv) supportive performance evidence including full-model AUROC=0.764 and an effect size OR=2.1 (top-vs-rest style implied by catalog effect size field). Key limitation: the reported AUROC appears to be a full-model metric (not explicitly PRS-only), and several other direct hypertension candidates also show competitive full-model AUROC (e.g., PGS004234 AUROC=0.763) or PRS-comparable metrics (e.g., PGS001320 includes PGS-only AUROC/R2 but comes from a pan-trait UKB framework), making the overall ranking not unequivocal; thus confidence is Moderate rather than High."
}

