  "outcome": "DIRECT_SUB_OPTIMAL",
  "best_model_id": "PGS001536",
  "confidence": "Moderate",
  "rationale": "All three candidates are labeled as vitiligo (direct trait_efo match), but they differ materially in endpoint fidelity and PRS-comparable performance evidence. PGS001536 is the only model reporting explicit PRS-only metrics (PGS AUROC (no covariates)=0.64193; PGS R2 (no covariates)=0.01621) plus incremental AUROC (0.08163) with clearly stated basic covariates; its PRS-only R2 is also plausibly below the provided vitiligo heritability ceiling (h2_obs=0.1738), supporting metric sanity. Limitations: it is a pan-trait UK Biobank framework score (“across 813 traits”), which the provided domain guidance flags as often less reliable externally, and its phenotype is time-to-event vitiligo rather than a straightforward case-control endpoint. The other two models have additional endpoint concerns: PGS000738 has phenotyping_reported='Red hair' despite vitiligo labeling and lacks PRS-only metrics; PGS000760’s phenotyping is 'anti-PD-L1 induced hypothyroidism in cancer patients', making it poorly aligned to vitiligo risk despite reporting an HR=1.41. Given these tradeoffs, PGS001536 is best supported among direct matches, but the framework origin and TTE endpoint keep this from a high-quality direct recommendation."
}

